01:35:32,055 --> 01:35:32,115
Aye.

1051
01:35:32,916 --> 01:35:33,596
The ayes have it.

1052
01:35:33,656 --> 01:35:34,637
Congratulations, Dan.

1053
01:35:34,677 --> 01:35:35,237
Thank you.

1054
01:35:35,257 --> 01:35:35,677
Thank you.

1055
01:35:36,337 --> 01:35:37,498
Ernie, sorry, I see your hand.

1056
01:35:37,538 --> 01:35:43,141
Lisa, does that mean, I know this is tongue in cheek, but will you have now time to co-chair?

1057
01:35:45,703 --> 01:35:48,364
You know what, I actually, we don't need to get into that now.

1058
01:35:48,404 --> 01:35:53,387
I believe the continuity of leadership is a really important thing.

1059
01:35:56,586 --> 01:35:57,707
So yes or no.

1060
01:35:58,387 --> 01:36:08,473
I know it's a no because I'm going to, if no one else does it, I'll nominate Jared because I think if he had, if he can do it, it's the continuity is really important.

1061
01:36:09,534 --> 01:36:12,276
You know, so if we have a new chair, I think it's great.

1062
01:36:12,296 --> 01:36:15,758
That's the way when, you know, Pat has been the co-chair.

1063
01:36:16,658 --> 01:36:19,040
And I, I, I think that's valuable.

1064
01:36:20,413 --> 01:36:29,032
Yeah, I was too sad that Jared wanted to step down, but I now realize that he's probably heard that one plus one equals three when it comes to.

1065
01:36:30,864 --> 01:36:37,648
So I've heard that one child takes up 95% of your time and the second one takes up the remaining 5%.

1066
01:36:37,688 --> 01:36:41,131
That's the remaining 95% of the time.

1067
01:36:41,171 --> 01:36:43,052
Takes up 150% of your time.

1068
01:36:43,072 --> 01:36:43,432
Yeah, maybe 150.

1069
01:36:43,472 --> 01:36:46,794
I actually have a question for Dennis.

1070
01:36:48,635 --> 01:36:52,778
So these meetings are all recorded, but we don't have transcripts, I believe.

1071
01:36:52,918 --> 01:36:55,620
Can we get transcription?

1072
01:36:57,162 --> 01:37:08,832
on the meetings and would that be beneficial to note-taking if so, so that if you miss something, you can at least plausibly go back and look at it.

1073
01:37:09,673 --> 01:37:11,154
That's a great question, P. Dan.

1074
01:37:11,695 --> 01:37:19,561
If we can get a digital copy of the recording, which I believe we can, there are actually like free software services that can transcribe and get Zoom to it.

1075
01:37:22,992 --> 01:37:25,273
I don't know, that would be nice if it would.

1076
01:37:25,433 --> 01:37:26,934
Google Meets does have a built-in.

1077
01:37:26,954 --> 01:37:29,195
Well, I know there are apps.

1078
01:37:29,215 --> 01:37:33,257
We can run it through deep speech.

1079
01:37:33,298 --> 01:37:40,201
I know there are apps you can add to Zoom that will just do live transcription and including live subtitles.

1080
01:37:40,781 --> 01:37:43,183
And then it says only if it airs on the public access channel live.

1081
01:37:43,703 --> 01:37:50,607
So if we do one of those and turn on subtitles, then maybe we can use that.

1082
01:37:51,437 --> 01:37:54,059
Yeah, maybe we can- It seems like a useful accessibility thing anyway, so.

1083
01:37:54,719 --> 01:37:55,820
Yeah, good idea.

1084
01:37:55,920 --> 01:37:59,523
We'll look at some other options for maybe making the note-taking process a little simpler.

1085
01:38:01,424 --> 01:38:12,212
Yeah, I'm willing to serve as vice chair, but I'm also willing to open it up if there's someone else who's really champing at the bit to serve in that role as well.

1086
01:38:14,174 --> 01:38:16,095
I think in terms of a chair,

1087
01:38:17,954 --> 01:38:20,236
I would nominate Emily for that.

1088
01:38:21,838 --> 01:38:28,064
You definitely carry the most stuff on a bike of anyone I know, so that's gotta be qualification for something.

1089
01:38:29,506 --> 01:38:37,774
But seriously, you're very competent and committed, and I think you very much walk the talk of what we do.

1090
01:38:39,295 --> 01:38:45,017
I mean, you also make my collection of bikes look paltry by comparison, which is an impressive feat.

1091
01:38:45,037 --> 01:38:49,019
I think you've got a lot of boots on the ground experience, and I think we do a very good job.

1092
01:38:49,519 --> 01:38:50,940
That doesn't mean that other people- You're not on the pedals, Jared.

1093
01:38:51,520 --> 01:38:51,860
What's that?

1094
01:38:52,280 --> 01:38:53,420
You mean on the pedals, Jared.

1095
01:38:55,561 --> 01:38:57,422
Yes, I can backstand well enough.

1096
01:38:57,482 --> 01:38:59,062
I don't need to put my boots on the ground.

1097
01:39:01,208 --> 01:39:04,251
I am willing to take over that role.

1098
01:39:04,271 --> 01:39:07,034
I've had a chat with Jared about it.

1099
01:39:07,054 --> 01:39:10,477
I'll second the nomination of Emily.

1100
01:39:13,460 --> 01:39:13,841
All right.

1101
01:39:14,381 --> 01:39:14,822
Well, look at that.

1102
01:39:14,862 --> 01:39:15,543
Move forward quickly.

1103
01:39:15,963 --> 01:39:18,646
All in favor of Emily serving as chair?

1104
01:39:19,106 --> 01:39:19,226
Aye.

1105
01:39:19,506 --> 01:39:19,587
Aye.

1106
01:39:19,607 --> 01:39:19,667
Aye.

1107
01:39:20,688 --> 01:39:21,428
The ayes have it.

1108
01:39:21,509 --> 01:39:22,409
Congratulations.

1109
01:39:22,590 --> 01:39:23,771
Well, I guess I'm done leading the meeting.

1110
01:39:23,831 --> 01:39:24,451
It's all on you now.

1111
01:39:26,368 --> 01:39:29,051
Oh, you can finish for the rest of this one.

1112
01:39:29,391 --> 01:39:29,871
Fair enough.

1113
01:39:30,072 --> 01:39:32,154
You can still get back to vice chair.

1114
01:39:33,315 --> 01:39:37,839
Which we did not actually have a motion for yet, or maybe we did, but it wasn't seconded.

1115
01:39:37,899 --> 01:39:39,961
Was there anyone else who really wanted to be vice chair?

1116
01:39:40,121 --> 01:39:41,883
I'll serve as vice chair.

1117
01:39:43,144 --> 01:39:43,464
Second.

1118
01:39:43,484 --> 01:39:46,687
All right, all in favor?

1119
01:39:47,468 --> 01:39:47,588
Aye.

1120
01:39:47,849 --> 01:39:47,989
Aye.

1121
01:39:48,129 --> 01:39:48,529
Aye.

1122
01:39:48,549 --> 01:39:49,850
All right.

1123
01:39:50,671 --> 01:39:51,292
Well, thank you all.

1124
01:39:52,316 --> 01:39:57,119
Thank you for understanding and being willing to have a bit of a reshuffle.

1125
01:39:57,640 --> 01:39:58,541
I do appreciate it.

1126
01:39:59,361 --> 01:40:00,242
Congratulations.

1127
01:40:00,862 --> 01:40:01,282
Thank you.

1128
01:40:02,143 --> 01:40:02,483
Thank you.

1129
01:40:02,724 --> 01:40:04,225
My wife appreciates it as well.

1130
01:40:05,886 --> 01:40:07,447
She's like, why haven't you already stepped out for this?

1131
01:40:07,507 --> 01:40:09,829
Come on.

1132
01:40:09,869 --> 01:40:10,229
Thank you all.

1133
01:40:13,348 --> 01:40:15,750
All right, well, that's down.

1134
01:40:16,651 --> 01:40:19,033
The other, well, we got a couple of other things here.

1135
01:40:20,414 --> 01:40:32,885
I'll run through these really quickly, but there's gonna be some new bike lanes on connecting Medford Square and the new train station, the GLX station, the Green Line.

1136
01:40:34,146 --> 01:40:39,270
That was presented, Todd and Amy presented that at the last Traffic Commission meeting.

1137
01:40:39,310 --> 01:40:41,612
Speaking of important meetings, there's going to be bike lanes

1138
01:40:42,492 --> 01:40:46,717
southbound on Main Street from around South Street.

1139
01:40:48,819 --> 01:40:54,786
Southbound, it's going to be mostly a bike lane there, southbound direction, Sharrows northbound.

1140
01:40:55,406 --> 01:40:57,028
Then once you get to George Street,

1141
01:40:58,155 --> 01:41:04,462
It will be sharrows westbound on George Street parking will remain on the north side of George Street.

1142
01:41:05,683 --> 01:41:16,834
It will be officially removed from the south side of the street apparently that wasn't allowed but the sign had been torn down at some point, so people weren't really sure you could park there or not.

1143
01:41:17,615 --> 01:41:21,958
But parking will be removed from the south side of George Street in between College and Maine.

1144
01:41:23,179 --> 01:41:30,204
There will be an eastbound bike lane there on George Street from College to Maine.

1145
01:41:31,405 --> 01:41:34,587
I would pull it up on the map, but I'm short for time.

1146
01:41:35,929 --> 01:41:48,602
And then there will be bike lanes, maybe a little bit of sheriffs but bike lanes the majority of North and South on college have between George and Boston.

1147
01:41:49,122 --> 01:41:52,285
So taking you to the new the new GLX station.

1148
01:41:53,126 --> 01:42:03,213
So it's not necessarily like the quietest, nicest way that some people might choose to ride, but it is making it clear that we expect there to be riders there.

1149
01:42:03,733 --> 01:42:09,337
And for people who enjoy a direct route, there's now going to be a bit of infrastructure to accommodate them.

1150
01:42:09,658 --> 01:42:18,804
And there will be requisite narrowing of vehicle lanes as well, down to 10 feet or so, which is about as narrow as you can get away with.

1151
01:42:19,958 --> 01:42:21,158
So very exciting.

1152
01:42:22,639 --> 01:42:33,902
The important thing to remember is that we will still have some opportunity to provide very specific feedback to Todd and Amy about what exactly the paint looks like and where it transitions and whatnot.

1153
01:42:35,342 --> 01:42:42,224
But they really just needed the Traffic Commission meeting to approve the general existence of these bike lanes and the removal of the parking.

1154
01:42:42,464 --> 01:42:45,585
That has been done, and that's great.

1155
01:42:45,685 --> 01:42:49,206
So thank you to those of you who were able to join that meeting.

1156
01:42:50,611 --> 01:42:51,531
speak in favor of that.

1157
01:42:52,652 --> 01:42:53,592
So exciting stuff.

1158
01:42:56,252 --> 01:42:58,373
Anything else on that before I move on?

1159
01:43:00,573 --> 01:43:02,194
All right.

1160
01:43:02,514 --> 01:43:04,054
We'll move this at a quicker pace here then.

1161
01:43:05,254 --> 01:43:06,575
Distribution of bike light kits.

1162
01:43:06,875 --> 01:43:10,275
Ernie, you have been going full force on putting these together.

1163
01:43:10,875 --> 01:43:12,316
Thank you so much for doing that.

1164
01:43:13,376 --> 01:43:17,497
What would be helpful, like you dropped some off at my house and those are just,

1165
01:43:18,237 --> 01:43:19,959
really, really, really awesome.

1166
01:43:19,999 --> 01:43:29,390
It's a little packet that's got front bike lights and some kind of useful pamphlets about how to bike in a city and how to stay involved in what's going on in the city.

1167
01:43:29,450 --> 01:43:34,996
So kudos to you for taking the initiative to do that and really getting it done.

1168
01:43:35,016 --> 01:43:38,359
I guess I wanted to chat with the group about

1169
01:43:39,440 --> 01:43:42,382
know, getting here from you, Ernie, exactly how many do we have?

1170
01:43:42,823 --> 01:43:43,543
Yeah, I have.

1171
01:43:43,703 --> 01:43:44,924
And how do we get them out to people?

1172
01:43:45,124 --> 01:43:46,405
Yeah, should we be focusing on?

1173
01:43:46,646 --> 01:43:47,967
Sure, I have a quick report.

1174
01:43:48,967 --> 01:43:50,228
So I designed them.

1175
01:43:50,268 --> 01:43:51,910
So they're for Medford only.

1176
01:43:52,565 --> 01:44:00,494
You know, as you can tell, both sides sort of restrict the distribution there because I don't want to be overextending us and that's not our purview.

1177
01:44:01,235 --> 01:44:10,806
I wonder if I could include in the kit a message from MBAC or the city or the mayor, just something to think about to address

1178
01:44:11,927 --> 01:44:15,729
The kids, I don't know if the chairs should be writing that.

1179
01:44:16,950 --> 01:44:22,632
As an aside, last week, the bike kitchen at Medford High did not get off the ground.

1180
01:44:22,652 --> 01:44:25,134
They, I think, plan to meet next week.

1181
01:44:25,494 --> 01:44:31,917
I was going to get active there and maybe get some people involved with the high school and distributing the lights, etc, etc.

1182
01:44:32,557 --> 01:44:35,118
To date, the 240 came in.

1183
01:44:35,238 --> 01:44:37,820
I have distributed personally 107 kits.

1184
01:44:40,801 --> 01:44:48,126
You know, maybe a third of them went to commission members, the rest to JRA.

1185
01:44:48,426 --> 01:44:50,327
I dropped some off at the police department.

1186
01:44:50,387 --> 01:44:55,211
I threw some in police SUVs, chatted them up.

1187
01:44:55,371 --> 01:44:56,572
There's some at the kitchen.

1188
01:44:56,592 --> 01:45:02,696
So there are 133 left that I'm assembling now because I've got more of those cards.

1189
01:45:03,536 --> 01:45:11,359
from Alicia's people and Dennis and Therese up there, the Medford Conference of Planned Cards, which I think are useful.

1190
01:45:11,379 --> 01:45:15,781
They get parents involved automatically through putting lights on with their kids.

1191
01:45:16,701 --> 01:45:20,763
So it looks like schools are a good venue there, chatting with the parents.

1192
01:45:20,843 --> 01:45:25,585
I've been meeting on the street with their kids and talking this up and all that.

1193
01:45:25,645 --> 01:45:32,588
They all suggest that we somehow get the schools involved and go to the schools and talk to kids, put lights on bikes.

1194
01:45:33,228 --> 01:45:40,953
We'll be doing that at Tufts Park with the helmet rodeo stuff next month so I think a bunch of them are going to go there.

1195
01:45:41,954 --> 01:45:46,597
JRA has have half funded the first set.

1196
01:45:46,917 --> 01:45:47,598
So I got $450 there.

1197
01:45:50,039 --> 01:45:51,580
As a matter of fact, today.

1198
01:45:51,600 --> 01:45:59,663
And Dennis has the bill for the rest of it, which will give us some money maybe to make the second purchase.

1199
01:45:59,683 --> 01:46:03,244
Remember, there's a month delay in getting these from China.

1200
01:46:03,924 --> 01:46:11,487
But I think that by the end of May, may run out of these and would want another 240 sets for the rest of the year.

1201
01:46:14,409 --> 01:46:28,878
I think a letter to any sponsor right now it's JRA and it's perhaps about to be Alewife Auto from the mayor or MBAC just as an appreciation for helping the kids in Medford with this is a good idea.

1202
01:46:28,898 --> 01:46:33,921
I don't know who can write that if the mayor can't get involved, maybe we can as a commission.

1203
01:46:35,664 --> 01:46:38,666
New members, would you please get me your addresses?

1204
01:46:39,086 --> 01:46:50,351
I can ride to you in the next couple of days and maybe drop off a half dozen kids at each of your addresses to put on kids' bikes or your own kids or whoever you know.

1205
01:46:51,032 --> 01:46:58,755
When I talk to kids, I tell them there are two requisites to getting these lights, that they wear a helmet all the time and they don't blink.

1206
01:46:59,456 --> 01:47:03,358
Then I go into a thing about dinosaurs and blinking and prey and all that.

1207
01:47:04,038 --> 01:47:06,299
Well, Ernie, I wanted to stop you real quick there.

1208
01:47:06,359 --> 01:47:07,319
That's it for my list.

1209
01:47:07,339 --> 01:47:08,599
So what do you have for questions?

1210
01:47:09,199 --> 01:47:16,901
Well, one thing I want us to think about is like the remainder that we have left, and I'd like us to maybe think strategically about who should get them.

1211
01:47:16,921 --> 01:47:22,003
You know, there may be some people who need them more than others, whether that's

1212
01:47:22,963 --> 01:47:27,886
people who live in certain poorer parts of the city or things like that.

1213
01:47:27,986 --> 01:47:30,987
There's probably different groups that might be good targets for that sort of thing.

1214
01:47:31,628 --> 01:47:34,669
I'm not sure exactly how to do it, but I'd like us to think about that.

1215
01:47:34,729 --> 01:47:41,573
Maybe reaching out to Kevin Bailey at the rec center might have his finger on the pulse for how to reach some of those people.

1216
01:47:41,593 --> 01:47:44,815
I just want to make sure we get the right distribution of those.

1217
01:47:45,996 --> 01:47:46,656
No, I agree.

1218
01:47:47,336 --> 01:47:50,218
When is our rodeo Tufts Park thing?

1219
01:47:51,618 --> 01:47:51,978
in May.

1220
01:47:52,279 --> 01:47:53,479
Is that scheduled already?

1221
01:47:54,400 --> 01:47:58,182
Yeah, so I think that's actually next on the agenda, right?

1222
01:47:58,562 --> 01:47:59,883
We only have a couple minutes left.

1223
01:48:00,143 --> 01:48:02,404
Do you want to transition into that?

1224
01:48:02,865 --> 01:48:05,406
You have any other questions, Jared, for me about the lights?

1225
01:48:06,587 --> 01:48:13,711
I would like to order the next round so that if we run out in a month, we're not left without any for the rest of the season.

1226
01:48:14,266 --> 01:48:25,611
Yeah, I think I'd like you to touch base with yet that was on the agenda to to touch base with Dennis figure out like I'm a little unclear on exactly how much money is left.

1227
01:48:25,691 --> 01:48:27,412
Yeah, I was there today.

1228
01:48:27,712 --> 01:48:29,573
I was there today and we went through that.

1229
01:48:30,173 --> 01:48:39,176
And with getting the 450 from JRA and the promise of another 450 from blah, blah, Dale Wife Auto, we're all clear.

1230
01:48:39,496 --> 01:48:42,817
I just wanted to make sure the money was spent before the fiscal year ends.

1231
01:48:43,418 --> 01:48:43,598
Right.

1232
01:48:43,638 --> 01:48:45,418
And we've got a grant.

1233
01:48:45,438 --> 01:48:50,020
So I want to place that order and get an invoice for the lights for what, May 30th?

1234
01:48:50,320 --> 01:48:51,580
Is that the deal?

1235
01:48:51,620 --> 01:48:53,401
Or is it June 30th, Dennis?

1236
01:48:55,702 --> 01:48:56,042
Dennis?

1237
01:48:57,695 --> 01:49:00,796
Oh, so you've seen my point.

1238
01:49:00,976 --> 01:49:01,816
I want to make sure.

1239
01:49:02,236 --> 01:49:10,898
And also he says that whatever we spend now, we should make sure we spend all of it, even more than we have, because that informs our allotment for the next year.

1240
01:49:10,918 --> 01:49:11,678
Right.

1241
01:49:12,078 --> 01:49:14,719
Anything you want to do is buy a lot of helmets.

1242
01:49:14,739 --> 01:49:19,260
Yeah, I was just going to say you had made a point about targeting the distribution.

1243
01:49:20,060 --> 01:49:24,121
And one of my interests in this is to have

1244
01:49:24,721 --> 01:49:27,406
actually be able to target them to adults as well as children.

1245
01:49:27,446 --> 01:49:33,696
I know that packets are oriented to children, but there's so many times when I see adults

1246
01:49:34,868 --> 01:49:37,350
who, for lack of better words, should know better.

1247
01:49:38,270 --> 01:49:46,676
And, you know, they're dressed darkly, they don't have any lights on, they think everybody can see them, and they're basically invisible riding their bikes on the street.

1248
01:49:46,696 --> 01:49:54,341
And somehow, I would like to be able to, you know, some of it I'm sure is just obstinance and other aspects are not

1249
01:49:55,202 --> 01:50:00,245
just not considering it, not getting it, not getting around to it, maybe not being able to afford it, I don't know.

1250
01:50:00,825 --> 01:50:15,873
But in any event, I'd like to suggest that we also, if we see an adult riding and have the wherewithal to approach them, that we provide the packet to them as well as necessarily kids who do it.

1251
01:50:19,313 --> 01:50:24,316
One of the reasons for distributing them to everybody was that hopefully you would all carry one around.

1252
01:50:24,356 --> 01:50:32,481
And when you see someone in need, you talk it up and give it to them, even perhaps put it on their bike if there's not a COVID risk, et cetera.

1253
01:50:33,061 --> 01:50:40,366
So that's my hope in sort of having all of us get around and spread these out to yes, people in need,

1254
01:50:41,226 --> 01:50:41,767
etc.

1255
01:50:42,007 --> 01:50:52,599
I'm a little low as to whether I want to approach someone without a helmet and put lights on their bike until they get a helmet on their bike, but that's a chicken egg thing.

1256
01:50:53,220 --> 01:50:55,042
Peter, you can't harm reduction.

1257
01:50:55,062 --> 01:50:59,066
An ounce of prevention is worth a pound of cure, so a light can help.

1258
01:50:59,647 --> 01:51:00,768
Yeah.

1259
01:51:00,808 --> 01:51:11,255
I don't know how to do that, Bruce, but the card that I included in the pack has the scan on the back for the Medford Comprehensive Involvement or whatever it's called.

1260
01:51:11,275 --> 01:51:15,979
That was the lure to try to get parents involved in other activities.

1261
01:51:16,039 --> 01:51:19,661
I didn't want this to be geared to just grade school kids.

1262
01:51:20,602 --> 01:51:27,828
but I see the looks on their faces when I give them each one of these little gusseted packets is remarkable.

1263
01:51:28,109 --> 01:51:30,330
They're extraordinarily appreciative.

1264
01:51:30,891 --> 01:51:35,995
They said they're not going to take the training wheels off and take biking seriously, put their helmet on all the time.

